# Gitleaks ignore rules.
#
# gitleaks 8.30.1 requires each entry here to be a full finding FINGERPRINT
# (format: rule-id:file:line:hash), NOT a bare secret value. The bare-value
# entries that used to live here (CI test keys such as ci-test-hmac-key-0001)
# stopped matching after the gitleaks upgrade and produced
# "Invalid .gitleaksignore entry" warnings on every scan (Issue #22).
#
# Those CI test values are now handled as precise, individually-anchored
# regexes in .gitleaks.toml [allowlist] instead - that is the format this
# gitleaks version supports and it keeps each exemption explicit and auditable.
#
# To ignore a NEW finding here, add its full fingerprint as printed by gitleaks,
# or prefer a narrowly-scoped regex in .gitleaks.toml [allowlist]. Never add a
# whole-file, whole-directory, or rule-wide exemption.